+A capability declaration is an offer, not the session contract. The server derives a **negotiated session contract** from every participant's capabilities plus the session requirements.
+
+The contract records which capabilities are required, optional, activated, rejected or available only through an explicitly approved fallback. Missing required semantics make the participant incompatible unless the active ruleset authorizes a typed fallback. Optional semantics are activated deterministically according to session policy.
+
+This lets an older or simpler game participate without making "ignore or approximate" an implicit rule for simulation-affecting behavior.
